WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.010
The invisible hand &amp; efficiency

2
00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:08.840
What does “efficient” mean here?

3
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:19.130
Total surplus (CS + PS) is maximised. Every unit left of Q* has MB above MC and is worth trading; every unit right of it costs more than it is worth.

4
00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:24.000
Define deadweight loss and how to compute it.

5
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:34.440
The surplus destroyed when the market does not trade the efficient quantity. On a graph, the triangle between D and S over the units that failed to trade: ½ × base × height.

6
00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:39.440
Pareto efficient vs. Pareto improvement?

7
00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:48.840
Pareto efficient: you cannot make anyone better off without making someone worse off. A Pareto improvement makes at least one person better off and nobody worse off.

8
00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:52.940
The equity–efficiency tradeoff?

9
00:00:52.940 --> 00:01:00.970
Efficiency is the size of total surplus; equity is who gets it. Economics alone cannot say which balance is right — that is normative.

10
00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:03.000
The invisible hand &amp; efficiency — 4 cards
